  "Delta vs v3 has no cause in the model. v4 is v3's run re-made at core 0.7.0 (M-2c-i): every v3 number is equal in v4's metrics and learner-swap files (a leaf walk over all of them; only the core version and the run time differ), and the model, SHAP and what-if bytes are identical. v4 adds what v3 had no slot for: the M-2b comparators (persistence, trend, per-segment base rates, calibration in the large) and M-2c-i's climatology at budget and paired interval.",
  "Climatology at budget (T11 at its terms; P2 gate III G-3): week-of-year climatology is scored at the model's budgets, each threshold fixed on validation by a climatology fit on train only (embargoed), then applied to test. Its scores tie in whole week-of-year groups, so its realised rates are not its nominal budgets. Read evaluation.climatology_alert_budgets beside alert_budgets, precision against the realised rate.",
  "The interval is crude and says so. The exemplar's test window holds 4 seasons, so only 35 distinct season-block draws exist, and one season (2021) carries most of the test positives. It describes these four seasons, not a population of seasons. The estimate is the full-test delta; the bounds are percentiles over seeded draws (evaluation_extras.paired_interval).",
